description:
At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

We are looking for a motivated and driven Global Accounting Process Owner - Finance Operations (m/f/d) to join our Global Accounting, Process Excellence Team. In this role, you'll help shape our team, drive the company to the next level, and have direct influence on our success. &nbsp;

About the Role

• Own and govern the global end-to-end accounting process, including standards, policies, procedures, and controls &nbsp;

• Drive global process harmonization and standardization across regions, business units, and shared service centres &nbsp;

• Lead process optimization initiatives, including native, robotic and agentive process automation, workflow optimization, and ERP enhancements &nbsp;

• Maintain the global process optimization roadmap, prioritize improvement opportunities, and manage implementation of approved initiatives &nbsp;

• Define and monitor process KPIs, service levels, and performance targets to ensure continuous improvement and value realization &nbsp;

• Ensure compliance with accounting policies, internal controls, audit requirements, and regulatory standards &nbsp;

• Partner with key stakeholders - including SSC, IT, country and regional teams, Product Owners, and external providers - to optimize end-to-end process performance &nbsp;

• Leverage process mining, analytics, and benchmarking to identify inefficiencies, root causes, and best practices &nbsp;

• Lead change management activities, including communication, training, and adoption of new processes and technologies &nbsp;

About You

• Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, Computer Science, or a related field . Advanced degree or relevant certifications (e.g., ACCA, CFA, CPA) are a plus .

• Big 4 experience ; Senior Manager level or above is preferr ed &nbsp;

• Experience delivering multi-country projects or transformation initiatives -i nternational assignment or secondment experience in Europe or North America preferred .

• Proven experience in leading Finance Transformation, Process Excellence, or Global Business Services (GBS) transformation programs

• Strong understanding of end-to-end accounting processes, with the ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions &nbsp;

• Experience working with ERP systems and finance technology tools; familiarity with process automation (RPA, APIs, workflow tools) is a plus &nbsp;

• Experience collaborating with product and engineering teams in an agile environment (e.g. , sprint reviews, roadmap planning) &nbsp;

• Strong stakeholder management and communication skills (Fluent in English (required), with the ability to operate effectively across global and local teams &nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

